<!--
  The real stack end to end, against the actual Gazebo/PX4 world — for a
  machine that can run them (see docs/LOCALIZATION.md's RAM note; this is
  NOT the RAM-constrained dev machine's demo_mission.launch.xml, which
  substitutes synthetic data specifically because Gazebo can't run there).

  Real: Localization (LiDAR/IMU -> FAST-LIO2 -> lio_state_bridge),
  World Model (real_world_model, clustering FAST-LIO2's own
  /cloud_registered — the actual live map, not a synthetic one), Mission
  (real_mission — waypoint-sequencing state machine, default params match
  the old golden scenario, see docs/MISSION.md), Planning (Theta* + D*
  Lite + CARM), Safety (real_safety — staleness/validity gating, an
  independent obstacle-clearance check, sustained-loss escalation to
  MODE_LAND, see docs/SAFETY.md). Still mocked: Vehicle/PX4 command
  interface — real_vehicle exists but is UNVERIFIED against real PX4
  (see docs/VEHICLE.md); swap it in manually once px4_msgs is vendored
  and you've confirmed the topic names/enum values against your PX4.

  RViz shows the SAME /viz/* topics as demo_mission.launch.xml
  (viz_bridge is demo-visualization-only, not part of any real module) —
  but every number behind them this time comes from the real sensors and
  the real vehicle in Gazebo, not from demo_world/demo_flyer.

  Prerequisites this launch file does NOT start for you (see
  docs/LOCALIZATION.md for the full, confirmed-working sequence):
    1. Gazebo running standalone with our world file
       (`gz sim -r simulation/worlds/x500_lidar.sdf`, GZ_SIM_RESOURCE_PATH
       including ~/.simulation-gazebo/models) in its own terminal, THEN PX4
       SITL with PX4_GZ_STANDALONE=1 and PX4_GZ_MODEL_NAME=x500_lidar_0
       (attaches to the statically-placed vehicle instead of spawning its
       own) in a second terminal — both steps required, in that order.
    2. simulation/launch/sensors_bridge.launch.xml running, to bridge the
       simulated sensors into /lidar/points and /imu/data.
    3. The vendored FAST-LIO2 backend built (uav_localization.repos).

  Mission goal: real_mission's default fixed target is (10, 0, 3) in the
  map frame — check that against where x500_lidar.sdf spawns the vehicle
  so the goal is actually reachable within the world's extent; override
  via a params file (see src/mission/uav_mission/config/) if not.
-->
<launch>
  <include file="$(find-pkg-share uav_localization)/launch/real_localization.launch.xml" />

  <node pkg="uav_world_model" exec="real_world_model" name="real_world_model" output="screen" />
  <node pkg="uav_mission" exec="real_mission" name="real_mission" output="screen" />
  <node pkg="uav_planning" exec="real_planner" name="real_planner" output="screen" />
  <node pkg="uav_safety" exec="real_safety" name="real_safety" output="screen" />
  <node pkg="uav_vehicle" exec="mock_vehicle" name="mock_vehicle" output="screen" />
  <node pkg="uav_bringup" exec="viz_bridge" name="viz_bridge" output="screen" />
  <node pkg="rviz2" exec="rviz2" name="rviz2"
        args="-d $(find-pkg-share uav_bringup)/config/viz.rviz" output="screen" />
</launch>
